<title>USA: Mafco Consolidated Group Inc Q3 net rises.</title>
<headline>Mafco Consolidated Group Inc Q3 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consolidated Statements Of Operations</p>
<p>	    Three Month Periods Ended  Nine Month Periods Ended</p>
<p>		    Sep 29,  Oct. 1,		Sep 29,   Oct. 1,</p>
<p>			 1996     1995		  1996	 1995</p>
<p> Net sales	$85,635  $68,679	     $230,380  $195,268</p>
<p> Operating income 23,922   10,737	     58,494    42,814</p>
<p>Gain on Cigar</p>
<p> Offering	  127,809	 --		127,809	  --</p>
<p>Income from continuing</p>
<p> operations	  98,025    3,944	     115,551    16,385</p>
<p>Discontinued operations</p>
<p> Net income	98,409    4,604		130,603    17,045</p>
<p>Income per share:</p>
<p> Continuing operations 4.22  0.17		  4.97	0.77</p>
<p>Discontinued</p>
<p>   operations	0.02     0.03		   0.65	0.03</p>
<p> Net Income	  4.24     0.20		   5.62	0.80</p>
<p>Weighted average common</p>
<p> shrs outstanding  23,237   23,482		 23,237  21,315</p>
<p>		    (In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: The full company name is Mafco Consolidated Group Inc.</p>
<p>In 96 Q3, income from continuing operations, excluding the after-tax gain of $83.1 million, or $3.58 per share, from the initial public offering of Consolidated Cigar Holdings was $14.9 million, or $0.64 per share, versus $3.9 million, or $0.17 per share, in 95 Q3. Net income in 96 Q3, excluding the after-tax gain on the Cigar IPO, was $15.3 million, or $0.66 per share, versus $4.6 million, or $0.20 per share, in the same period in 1995.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
